  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Create three DataGrid config template JSON files under `scripts/config-templates/` (directory does not exist yet). Update `docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md` § Step 2 to reference them as the recommended starting point for makers.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE maker-experience contributor. Understands the DataGrid framework configuration schema thoroughly. Reads `DataGridConfiguration.ts` to ensure templates parse against the current type.
  </role>

  <goal>
    3 JSON files exist under `scripts/config-templates/`. Each is a valid `sprk_configjson` payload against the current TypeScript type. Guide references them.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      DataGrid config has ~9 top-level keys with 30+ nested fields. Makers today either copy from an existing record, read the 400+ line TS type, or read the comprehensive guide. FR-06 provides three template starting points sized to common shapes: minimum viable, drill-through, and full-featured.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>scripts/config-templates/entity-list-basic.json (NEW)</file>
      <file>scripts/config-templates/entity-list-drill-through.json (NEW)</file>
      <file>scripts/config-templates/entity-list-full.json (NEW)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/DataGridConfiguration.ts (reference — schema type)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md (modified — § Step 2)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Each JSON must parse against the current `DataGridConfiguration` TypeScript type (verified via `tsc --noEmit` or a quick script).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Templates use placeholder IDs (e.g., `"<entity-name>"`, `"<savedquery-id>"`) that makers replace.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`_version: "1.0"` in all three (no version bump).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>`scripts/config-templates/` does not exist. No overlap.</existing>
    <extension>N/A — brand new directory + files.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>New maker onboarding takes 2+ hours to author a config from scratch (read 400-line TS type + reverse-engineer working record); templates cut this to ~15 min. Concrete failure = onboarding friction + inconsistent record shapes across makers.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/DataGridConfiguration.ts</file>
      <file>docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-06 + review `DataGridConfiguration.ts` to catalog required + optional fields.</step>
    <step order="2">Create `scripts/config-templates/entity-list-basic.json`: minimum viable — `_version`, `source` (savedquery), `display` (title, columns), `rowOpen` (default modal), `behavior.pageSize`. Use `<entity-name>` + `<savedquery-id>` placeholders. Add a top-level `$comment` explaining purpose + replacement instructions.</step>
    <step order="3">Create `scripts/config-templates/entity-list-drill-through.json`: adds parent-context filter (`source.parentContext`), explicit column overrides (`columns[]`), and `secondaryActions[]`. Same placeholder convention.</step>
    <step order="4">Create `scripts/config-templates/entity-list-full.json`: every field with sensible defaults. Add per-field `$comment` describing purpose. Include new R2 fields (`availableViews`, `contentSizing` on section metadata — but note the section-metadata field is on the section registration, not the config; keep template scoped to `sprk_configjson`).</step>
    <step order="5">Verify all three JSONs parse against the type: write a tiny Node script (or use `ts-node`) that imports the type + JSON.parse's each file + assigns to the type. Or use `tsc` with `--allowJs` + JSDoc type-checking. Fastest: add a Vitest to `Spaarke.UI.Components` that parses + type-asserts each template.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md` § Step 2 (Author a new config record): add a subsection referencing the three templates with 1-line each on when to use.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: status → ✅ completed.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Type-check / test JSON parses against schema</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Create files</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">scripts/config-templates/entity-list-basic.json (new)</output>
    <output type="config">scripts/config-templates/entity-list-drill-through.json (new)</output>
    <output type="config">scripts/config-templates/entity-list-full.json (new)</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md (modified — § Step 2)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">3 JSON files exist under `scripts/config-templates/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each JSON parses against `DataGridConfiguration` TypeScript type without errors (verified via type-check script or Vitest).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each JSON contains `"_version": "1.0"` and placeholder markers (`<entity-name>`, `<savedquery-id>`) for maker substitution.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Configuration guide § Step 2 references the templates with a 1-line description each.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    - Directory `scripts/config-templates/` doesn't exist yet — create it.
    - Templates target makers, not developers — keep JSON readable + comments generous.
    - JSON doesn't support comments; use `$comment` string keys (jq-friendly pattern) — the schema tolerates extra keys since `sprk_configjson` runtime ignores unknown keys.
  </notes>

